# core.autocrlf=true hands Windows checkouts CRLF, but gofmt only ever writes
# LF. Files git checked out then disagree with files an editor wrote directly,
# so `gofmt -l` reports a file whose committed bytes are already correct — a
# lint failure with nothing to fix and no possible commit.
#
# text=auto still detects binaries and leaves them alone, so this one line
# covers every text file without listing extensions.
* text=auto eol=lf
